velt/package: the type of the package manifest, `package.velt` (docs/tooling/manifest.md).

Types only. `velt` never compiles a manifest: it reads it as data (vpm::manifest::read). These
types give editors completion, hover and errors while writing one:

  import type { Package } from "velt/package";

  export const pkg: Package = { name: "hello", version: "0.1.0" };

Prelude: assertions for tests and invariants. A failed one throws an `AssertionError`, as
Node's `assert` does: `velt test` reports it as the test's failure and runs the next test;
elsewhere it is an uncaught error like any other (exit code 1).

